        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): approve, reject, and remove device pairings from the phone",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Android Nodes & Devices screen shows pending device-pair counts but offers no actions — it tells the user to run a CLI command on the gateway host. Approving a new device is exactly the moment the operator is often *not* at that host; the already-trusted phone in their pocket is the natural place to act, and the gateway has exposed `device.pair.list/approve/reject/remove` for it all along.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPhone-side pairing administration, built to the gateway's actual authorization contract:\n\n- **Approve / Reject** for pending requests, gated on hello `features.methods` plus granted scopes (`operator.pairing` or admin) — and per row on the gateway's *second* gate: a caller who cannot grant the request's roles/scopes (verified against `server-methods/devices.ts` and `infra/device-pairing.ts`, cited in-source) sees Approve disabled instead of a doomed button.\n- **Remove** for paired devices, admin-gated to match the gateway's removal contract (non-admin removal is self-only for operator-only pairings, which Android pairings never are).\n- **Consent integrity**: the approve dialog is the consent surface, so it renders the complete requested roles/scopes — unbounded, scrollable, control/bidi-sanitized (a requester must not hide `operator.admin` behind a truncation ellipsis). Display names keep a cosmetic length cap.\n- **Truthful outcomes**: mutations capture the gateway scope at claim time (device ids recur across gateways — a reconnect must never route the request to a replacement gateway), require the exact write acknowledgement plus a canonical `device.pair.list` readback before reporting success, surface definitive gateway denials verbatim, and reserve the generic \"could not verify\" for genuinely ambiguous outcomes. The verified snapshot takes over the refresh generation so an in-flight refresh can't republish pre-mutation state, and pending confirmations are keyed to the gateway identity so they die on gateway switch.\n- **Scope discipline**: the bootstrap-requested scope set stays exactly the canonical limited profile (regression-tested) — limited QR onboarding is unaffected. The pairing UI lights up for sessions that already hold pairing/admin (full-access bootstraps, admin operators). Extending the limited mobile bootstrap profile with `operator.pairing` is a gateway-side product decision deliberately left open, noted at the capability selector.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators with full-access or admin sessions can approve, reject, and remove device pairings directly from the phone, with the requesting device's identity and complete requested access shown before approval. Limited sessions keep the existing CLI guidance. 24 new strings, translated across all 21 locales.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `GatewayDevicePairingTest` + `GatewayDevicePairingRuntimeTest` (capability gating incl. second-gate scope math, request params, ack echo + readback verification, definitive-denial vs ambiguous outcomes, long-scope visibility, identity sanitization), `NodesDevicesSettingsScreenTest`, `GatewayBootstrapAuthTest` (bootstrap set matches canonical limited profile), `ConnectionManagerTest`, `GatewaySessionInvokeTest`: green (Play flavor; ThirdParty compile green).\n- `:app:ktlintCheck`, `android-app-i18n` check, `git diff --check`: green.\n- RPC shapes verified against gateway source: `core-descriptors.ts:228-231`, `schema/devices.ts:13-23`, `server-methods/devices.ts` (list/approve/reject/remove responses; approval role/scope checks at :268/:314; removal contract at :441-478; requested-scope check in `infra/device-pairing.ts:854`).\n- Structured autoreview: eight rounds; seven accepted findings fixed (consent-surface truncation, second-gate row eligibility, bootstrap-profile regression, non-admin Remove exposure, refresh-race trio across mutation/refresh/dialog lifecycles); final round clean at 0.98 across all three chunks.\n",
        "branch": "feat/android-pairing-actions",
